title: Deepfake
text: Two identical portraits in yellow, and not a drop of yellow paint on the board. Only one of them is what it seems to be.
trick: the fixed prism under the right portrait only gives a single yellow beam if red arrives along the row and green from the south-east; the left portrait is the fake, lit only where those same red and green beams cross on their way there, so the forgery lies on the road to the original
motif: pictogram (two identical portraits with slotted frames, a fixed prism as the camera, and a plate for the blue left over)
expect: recolours>=1
proof: not proved; no other solution found in 300 s
---
